        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(config): warn when JSON5 comments are lost on config write",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw parses `openclaw.json` using JSON5, which supports comments. However, when the configuration is modified, the system saves back using standard `JSON.stringify()`, which strips all user-authored comments.\n\n**Issue**: #105683\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe root cause is in `src/config/io.ts` where config writes use `JSON.stringify()` which cannot preserve JSON5 comments.\n\nThis PR implements a warning to notify users when their comments will be lost.\n\n## User Impact\n\n### Before\n- Users add comments to `openclaw.json` for documentation\n- Any config modification silently strips all comments\n\n### After  \n- Users receive a clear warning when writing config with JSON5 comments\n- The warning intelligently excludes false positives (URLs in strings)\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Implementation\n\n1. **New `hasJSON5Comments()` function** (`src/config/io.ts`):\n   - Strips string literals using regex\n   - Detects `//` and `/*` comment markers\n   - Avoids false positives on URLs\n\n2. **Warning logic**:\n   - Checks if original config has JSON5 comments before writing\n   - Provides actionable guidance to users\n\n3. **Comprehensive tests** (`src/config/io.write-config.test.ts`):\n   - All 69 tests pass\n   - Covers comment detection, no-comment configs, URL edge cases\n\n### Code Quality\n\n- TypeScript compliant (no `any` types)\n- Format check passes\n- Follows existing patterns\n\n## Related Work\n\nAddresses issue #105683 and builds upon PR #105727 approach.",
